          "physical_scope": "A constructed units-labelled tangent-cone optimization illustration with one zero-amount boundary; it makes no thermodynamic-equilibrium, material, or empirical claim.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Use species $A,B$, one reaction column $\\nu=(-1,1)^{\\mathsf T}$, and starting amounts $n_A^0=0$ mol, $n_B^0=1$ mol. The admissible extents are $\\xi\\in[-1,0]$ mol because $n_A(\\xi)=-\\xi$ and $n_B(\\xi)=1\\,\\mathrm{mol}+\\xi$ must both be nonnegative. Let $\\Phi_0$ have units joules and define an ambient affine potential on an open neighborhood of the nonnegative amount region by\n$$\n\\widehat\\Phi(n_A,n_B)=\\Phi_0+1\\,\\mathrm J-(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}})n_B .\n$$\nAlong $n(\\xi)=(-\\xi,1\\,\\mathrm{mol}+\\xi)$, set $\\Phi(\\xi):=\\widehat\\Phi(n(\\xi))=\\Phi_0-(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}})\\xi$. Its derivative-defined amount coefficients are $\\mu_A:=\\partial_{n_A}\\widehat\\Phi=0$ and $\\mu_B:=\\partial_{n_B}\\widehat\\Phi=-1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$, including at $\\xi_*=0$ mol. This ambient extension is constructed optimization data only; no positive-mole thermodynamic chart at $n_A=0$ or physical realization is asserted.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
