          "physical_scope": "A constructed continuous entropy extension that is positive and concave on a convex ambient domain but restricted to a noncompact generator set omitting its maximizing barycenter; it makes no material claim.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, let $K\\subseteq C\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ with $K$ noncompact and $C$ convex, and let $\\mathcal P$ be a nonempty family of Borel probability measures on $K$ sharing a prescribed barycenter. The statement refuted is that $\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P}\\int_Ks\\,dP$ is always attained whenever $s=\\widetilde s|_K$ for a bounded, positive, continuous concave function $\\widetilde s:C\\to\\mathbb R$. Here convexity of $C$ means $(1-t)x+ty\\in C$ for $x,y\\in C$ and $t\\in[0,1]$, and concavity means\n$$\n\\widetilde s((1-t)x+ty)\\ge(1-t)\\widetilde s(x)+t\\widetilde s(y)\\qquad(x,y\\in C,\\ t\\in[0,1]).\n$$",
          "provenance": {
