          },
          "physical_scope": "A constructed pair of one-component Gibbs charts satisfying the same-tag, exchange, and reversible-heat assumptions of the local Clapeyron theorem; the constants are illustrative and are not observations.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix $T_0=300\\,\\mathrm K$, $p_0=10^5\\,\\mathrm{Pa}$, $g_0=1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$, $c>0$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, and $\\kappa>0$ in $\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}Pa^{-1}}$. On a common open chart define\n$$\ng_i(T,p)=g_0-s_i(T-T_0)-\\frac{c}{2T_0}(T-T_0)^2+v_i(p-p_0)-\\frac{\\kappa}{2}(p-p_0)^2,\n$$\nfor $i\\in\\{\\alpha,\\beta\\}$, with $s_\\alpha=2\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, $s_\\beta=5\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, $v_\\alpha=1.0\\times10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}}$, and $v_\\beta=4.0\\times10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}}$. Set $G_i=n_i g_i$ and use the natural Gibbs assignments $S_i=-\\partial_TG_i$, $V_i=\\partial_pG_i$, $\\mu_i=\\partial_{n_i}G_i$, and $U_i=G_i+TS_i-pV_i$. Thus same-tag homogeneity is explicit. Assume the constructed model stipulates an attained coexistence endpoint with bilateral energy, volume, and species exchange, and a reversible $\\alpha\\to\\beta$ conversion in contact with an ideal thermal reservoir at $T_0$. The reversible conversion is a record of the complete finite isolated compound comprising converted phases, the fixed-temperature reservoir, work stores and all auxiliaries, with equilibrium endpoints and additive component entropy. Every component other than the converted phases and reservoir has zero entropy change, and the reservoir change is $-Q/T_0$. These are the exact additional entropy premises of the local Clapeyron theorem. These parameters and endpoint assumptions are model inputs, not empirical claims.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
