          "title": "Fixed-frequency reciprocal tensor medium",
          "statement": "Fix a real angular frequency $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R$ and a bounded open region $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^3$ with $C^1$ boundary in a material-rest frame. Here a material-rest frame is the inertial frame in which every modelled material element has fixed spatial coordinates, as stipulated by the framework's material-closure postulate. A map in $C^1(\\overline\\Omega)$ means the restriction of a $C^1$ map on an open neighborhood of $\\overline\\Omega$. Let $\\varepsilon,\\mu:\\overline\\Omega\\to\\mathbb C^{3\\times3}$ be continuous coefficient fields with units $\\mathrm{F\\,m^{-1}}$ and $\\mathrm{H\\,m^{-1}}$. They may be spatially varying and complex. Let $E_j,H_j\\in C^1(\\overline\\Omega;\\mathbb C^3)$ and $J_j\\in C^0(\\overline\\Omega;\\mathbb C^3)$, for $j=1,2$, be phasor amplitudes with SI units $\\mathrm{V\\,m^{-1}}$, $\\mathrm{A\\,m^{-1}}$, and $\\mathrm{A\\,m^{-2}}$. The corresponding real fields use $e^{-i\\omega t}$, for example $E_j^{\\mathrm{real}}(x,t)=\\operatorname{Re}(E_j(x)e^{-i\\omega t})$. Their displacement and magnetic-induction amplitudes are $D_j=\\varepsilon E_j$ in $\\mathrm{C\\,m^{-2}}$ and $B_j=\\mu H_j$ in $\\mathrm T$.\n\nThe fixed-frequency constitutive and source equations are\n\n$$D_j=\\varepsilon E_j,\\qquad B_j=\\mu H_j,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}E_j=i\\omega B_j,\\qquad \\operatorname{curl}H_j=J_j-i\\omega D_j.$$\n\nAll operators act componentwise on the spatial variable. For $u,v\\in\\mathbb C^3$, define the **bilinear** dot product $u\\cdot v=\\sum_{r=1}^3u_rv_r$ and the complex-bilinear cross product by the usual right-handed component formula. Neither product conjugates either input. The transpose $T$ is the ordinary matrix transpose, without complex conjugation. This definition calls the coefficient model **reciprocal** when $\\varepsilon(x)^T=\\varepsilon(x)$ and $\\mu(x)^T=\\mu(x)$ at every $x\\in\\overline\\Omega$. It places no Hermitian, positive-definite, or passivity condition on these complex matrices.\n\nThis is a fixed-frequency phasor data class. Its possibly complex coefficients are not inferred from the framework's real, instantaneous material branch; a separate response model is required to justify any such interpretation.",
