          "id": "def-emx-matrix-maxwell-system",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite compatible matrix system",
          "statement": "Let $n_e,n_b,n_c,n_g$ be nonnegative integers. For dimension zero, $\\mathbb R^0$ has its single empty vector and its unique square matrix acts as the identity on that space. Choose real matrices $M_e\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e\\times n_e}$ and $M_b\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b\\times n_b}$ that are symmetric positive definite, meaning $M_e^T=M_e$, $M_b^T=M_b$, $x^TM_ex>0$ for every nonzero $x\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e}$, and $y^TM_by>0$ for every nonzero $y\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b}$; these positivity conditions are vacuous on $\\mathbb R^0$. Choose $C\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b\\times n_e}$, a symmetric positive semidefinite $S\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e\\times n_e}$, meaning $S^T=S$ and $x^TSx\\ge0$ for every $x\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e}$, and matrices $D\\in\\mathbb R^{n_c\\times n_b}$ and $G\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e\\times n_g}$ satisfying $DC=0$ and $CG=0$. These are finite real matrix data; no mesh or continuum field is assumed.\n\nLet $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, let $j:I\\to\\mathbb R^{n_e}$ be continuous, and let candidate states $e:I\\to\\mathbb R^{n_e}$ and $b:I\\to\\mathbb R^{n_b}$ be of class $C^1$. The **finite compatible matrix system** is\n\n$$M_e\\dot e(t)=C^TM_bb(t)-Se(t)-j(t),\\qquad \\dot b(t)=-Ce(t)\\quad(t\\in I).$$\n\nIts quadratic **energy** is $W(e,b):=\\tfrac12(e^TM_ee+b^TM_bb)$. Its magnetic constraint is the vector $Db\\in\\mathbb R^{n_c}$. For the chosen $G$, its weak-divergence coordinate is $q:=-G^TM_ee\\in\\mathbb R^{n_g}$. The term “weak-divergence” names this finite-dimensional quantity only. If the columns of $G$ form a basis of $\\ker C:=\\{v\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e}:Cv=0\\}$, then $q=0$ exactly when $M_ee\\in\\operatorname{im}C^T:=\\{C^Tu:u\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b}\\}$.",
          "deps": [
            "thm-finite-dimensional-orthogonal-decomposition"
          ],
