        {
          "id": "thm-emx-matrix-energy-constraints",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Energy, existence and algebraic constraints",
          "statement": "For the finite compatible matrix system on an open interval $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$, let $t_0\\in I$, choose initial data $e(t_0)=e_0$ and $b(t_0)=b_0$, and assume the forcing $j:I\\to\\mathbb R^{n_e}$ is continuous. There is a unique $C^1$ solution $(e,b)$ on all of $I$. At every $t\\in I$ it satisfies\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}W(e(t),b(t))=-e(t)^TSe(t)-e(t)^Tj(t),\\qquad Db(t)=Db(t_0),\\qquad \\dot q(t)=G^T(Se(t)+j(t)).$$",
