        {
          "id": "alg-emx-staggered-leapfrog",
          "kind": "algorithm",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Staggered compatible leapfrog",
          "statement": "Inputs are real matrices $M_e\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e\\times n_e}$ and $M_b\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b\\times n_b}$ that are symmetric positive definite, $C\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b\\times n_e}$, and compatible matrices $D,G$ satisfying $DC=CG=0$, with $S=0$ and $j\\equiv0$ in the finite compatible matrix system. All dimensions are nonnegative integers as in that system. Also input a real step size $h>0$, an integer horizon $N\\ge0$, and initial vectors $e_0\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e}$ and $b_{-1/2}\\in\\mathbb R^{n_b}$. The matrix $M_e$ is positive definite, so each mass equation below has a unique exact solution, including the unique empty solve when $n_e=0$. For each integer $n=0,1,\\ldots,N-1$, first set\n\n$$b_{n+1/2}:=b_{n-1/2}-hCe_n,$$\n\nthen solve uniquely for $v_n\\in\\mathbb R^{n_e}$ in\n\n$$M_ev_n=C^TM_bb_{n+1/2}$$\n\nand set $e_{n+1}:=e_n+h v_n$. Output the electric vectors $e_0,e_1,\\ldots,e_N$ and magnetic vectors $b_{-1/2},b_{1/2},\\ldots,b_{N-1/2}$. When $N=0$, the loop makes no updates and the output consists only of the two initial vectors. Every mass solve is exact; no inexact-solve error model is part of this procedure.",
