          "statement": "Fix $\\sigma\\in\\{+1,-1\\}$ and $0<\\theta_0<\\pi$. Let $\\gamma(t)=(\\theta_0,2\\pi t)$ for $0\\le t\\le1$ be the latitude loop in the direction sphere, and set $\\Omega:=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_0^{\\theta_0}\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta\\,d\\phi=2\\pi(1-\\cos\\theta_0)$, the outward solid angle of its north cap. The spherical gauge gives $\\mathrm{Hol}_\\gamma=\\exp(i2\\pi\\sigma\\cos\\theta_0)$. The north-pole regular gauge $v_N=e^{i\\sigma\\phi}v_\\sigma$ has $A_N=\\sigma(\\cos\\theta-1)d\\phi$ and is smooth on the cap; its loop integral and the cap flux are both $-\\sigma\\Omega$. Hence $\\mathrm{Hol}_\\gamma=\\exp(-i\\sigma\\Omega)=\\exp(i2\\pi\\sigma\\cos\\theta_0)$.",
