          "statement": "Let $m=|q|>0$ in the one-hole Reissner–Nordström (RN) conformal-data family; this equality defines its extremal parameter case. Use the punctured spatial manifold $\\Sigma=(0,\\infty)\\times S^2$. Then $\\psi^2=1+m/r$, $h:=\\psi^4(dr^2+r^2\\gamma_{S^2})$, and the centered sphere is $S_r:=\\{r\\}\\times S^2$, with areal radius $\\rho(r):=r\\psi^2=r+m$. On each $S_r$ use the outward unit normal $\\nu:=\\psi^{-2}\\partial_r$ and define the mean-curvature scalar $H:=\\operatorname{div}_h\\nu$; a sphere is minimal exactly when $H=0$. With this convention, no centered coordinate sphere is minimal. The proper radial coordinate\n\n$$s(r):=r+m\\log(r/m)$$\n\nhas range $\\mathbb R$ and gives\n\n$$h=ds^2+(r(s)+m)^2\\gamma_{S^2}.$$\n\nAs $r\\downarrow0$, $s\\to-\\infty$ and $r(s)+m\\to m$, so this end is asymptotic to the product cylinder $\\mathbb R\\times S^2$ with round-sphere radius $m$. The puncture is omitted; no point-source interpretation or global event-horizon claim is part of this example.\n\n",
