            "alg-emg-fx-leapfrog-cochains": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "physical_scope": null,
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "For rational admissible input matrices and initial state, positive rational step size $\\tau$, and finite $N\\geq0$, the specified finite leapfrog algorithm returns after finitely many exact rational arithmetic operations, with the stated $N+1$ states and the exact rational inverse $M_1^{-1}$. A dense implementation uses $O(n_1^3)$ rational arithmetic operations for the one-time elimination and $O(n_1^2+n_1n_2+n_2^2)$ per update. Retaining all input matrices $D_0,D_1,D_2,M_1,M_2$, the computed inverse, and all $N+1$ states uses $O(n_1n_0+n_1^2+n_1n_2+n_2^2+n_2n_3+(N+1)(n_1+n_2))$ rational entries. These are arithmetic-operation and storage counts only; they give no bound on rational bit growth, floating-point roundoff, linear-solve residuals, or continuum accuracy.",
          "library": "mathematics",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
