          "statement": "Take $M=\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^3$ with length-valued coordinates\n$(t,\\mathbf x)$, Lorentzian metric $g=-dt^2+d\\mathbf x^2$, and time\norientation $N=\\partial_t$. For $\\mathbf x\\ne0$, set\n$r:=|\\mathbf x|$ and\n$\\partial_r:=\\sum_{i=1}^3(x^i/r)\\partial_{x^i}$. For $R>0$, let\n$$S=\\{(0,R\\omega):\\omega\\in\\mathbb S^2\\}.$$\nThe future null normals\n$\\ell=\\partial_t+\\partial_r$ and $k=\\partial_t-\\partial_r$ satisfy\n$g(\\ell,k)=-2$ and have expansions\n$$\\theta_\\ell=\\frac2R,\\qquad \\theta_k=-\\frac2R.$$\nAlong the inward congruence generated by $k$, the screen Jacobi map is\n$A_\\lambda=(1-\\lambda/R)\\operatorname{id}$, so its first focal instant is\n$\\lambda=R$. The affine focusing bound from\n[[prop-gr-fx-null-raychaudhuri]] is attained, and every point\n$\\gamma_\\omega(\\lambda)=(\\lambda,(R-\\lambda)\\omega)$ with\n$R<\\lambda<3R$ lies in $I^+(S)$.",
