          "physical_scope": "A fixed-chart equality of asymptotic limits under compactly supported metric changes; no field equation or positivity result is used.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $h$ and $h'$ be two $C^2$ Riemannian metrics on the same end $E=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:r=|x|>R_0\\}$, with the same fixed Cartesian chart and asymptotic time normalization stated below. Suppose $h=h'$ outside a compact set $C\\subset E$ and both fixed-chart ADM limits exist. Then\n$$E_{\\mathrm{ADM}}(h;x)=E_{\\mathrm{ADM}}(h';x).$$\nThe symmetric tensors $K$ associated with the two data sets may differ; each need only satisfy the decay in the definition.",
