{
      "id": "gr-fx05-bondi-news-and-memory",
      "title": "Null infinity, Bondi news and classical memory",
      "kind": "A",
      "category": "general-relativity",
      "library": "physics",
      "companion": "gr-fx05-bondi-news-and-memory-examples",
      "requires": [
        "gr-fx01-hypersurface-and-null-geometry",
        "gr-linearized-waves",
        "gr-curvature-and-tides"
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "A smooth vacuum Bondi expansion",
          "reference": "items/def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 draft authored; readiness recorded separately.",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-gr-fx-null-screen-geometry",
            "def-gr-wave-screen-and-tt-projection",
            "def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-gr-fx-null-screen-geometry": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-gr-wave-screen-and-tt-projection": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "physical_scope": "Formal smooth asymptotically flat vacuum Bondi data at a null end; no global vacuum existence, exact finite-radius waveform, empirical claim, or conclusion about nature is asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth Lorentzian tangent-bundle conventions of the suppliers. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval, $r_0>0$, and $\\mathcal E=I\\times(r_0,\\infty)\\times S^2$, where $S^2=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^3:|x|=1\\}$ has its unit round metric $q_{AB}$ and area form $d\\Omega$. Let $D_A$ be the Levi-Civita covariant derivative of $q$, and raise angular indices with $q^{AB}$. A **Bondi-Sachs end** is a smooth Lorentzian metric on $\\mathcal E$ written in coordinates $(u,r,x^A)$, $A,B=1,2$, as\n\n$$g=-\\left(e^{2\\beta}\\frac Vr-r^2\\gamma_{AB}U^AU^B\\right)du^2-2e^{2\\beta}du\\,dr-2r^2\\gamma_{AB}U^Bdu\\,dx^A+r^2\\gamma_{AB}dx^A dx^B,$$\n\nwhere $\\beta,V,U^A,\\gamma_{AB}$ are smooth, $\\gamma_{AB}$ is positive definite, $\\gamma^{AC}\\gamma_{CB}=\\delta^A_B$, and $\\det(\\gamma_{AB})=\\det(q_{AB})$. Thus $u=\\mathrm{constant}$ are outgoing null hypersurfaces, $r$ is the area radius, and $x^A$ are constant along their null generators. This Bondi gauge has $g_{rr}=g_{rA}=0$.\n\nA **smooth Bondi expansion** is such an end with the differentiated uniform expansions\n\n$$\\gamma_{AB}=q_{AB}+\\frac{C_{AB}(u,x)}r+\\frac{P_{AB}(u,x)}{r^2}+O(r^{-3}),\\qquad \\beta=O(r^{-2}),\\qquad U^A=\\frac{U^A_{(2)}(u,x)}{r^2}+\\frac{U^A_{(3)}(u,x)}{r^3}+O(r^{-4}),\\qquad V=r-2m(u,x)+\\frac{V_{(1)}(u,x)}r+O(r^{-2}).$$\n\nHere $C_{AB}$, $P_{AB}$ and the displayed coefficients are smooth sphere fields on $I$; the determinant gauge imposes $q^{AB}C_{AB}=0$ and $q^{AB}P_{AB}=\\tfrac12 C_{AB}C^{AB}$. For every compact $I'\\subset I$, angular chart compact set, and derivative multi-index $\\alpha$ of total order at most two, the partial derivatives of each $O(r^{-k})$ remainder obey $\\partial_u^{\\alpha_u}D^{\\alpha_x}\\partial_r^{\\alpha_r}O(r^{-k})=O(r^{-k-\\alpha_r})$ uniformly as $r\\to\\infty$. Define the **mass aspect** by $m(u,x):=-\\tfrac12\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}(V(u,r,x)-r)$, the **Bondi shear** by $C_{AB}=\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}r(\\gamma_{AB}-q_{AB})$, the **Bondi news** by $N_{AB}:=\\partial_u C_{AB}$, and the **geometric Bondi mass** by $m_B(u):=\\frac1{4\\pi}\\int_{S^2}m(u,x)\\,d\\Omega$. The future null boundary used here is the formal $r\\to\\infty$ boundary $\\mathcal I^+=I\\times S^2$ with coordinates $(u,x^A)$; no conformal completion is included in this definition.\n\nA **vacuum Bondi expansion** is a smooth Bondi expansion whose Ricci tensor vanishes identically on the supplied end: $\\operatorname{Ric}_g(p)=0$ for every $p\\in\\mathcal E$. Equivalently, $\\operatorname{Ric}_{ab}(u,r,x)=0$ for every pair $a,b\\in\\{u,r,1,2\\}$ at every point of every Bondi coordinate chart, with no cosmological term. The curvature convention is $R(X,Y)Z=\\nabla_X\\nabla_YZ-\\nabla_Y\\nabla_XZ-\\nabla_{[X,Y]}Z$, $R(\\partial_c,\\partial_d)\\partial_b=R^a{}_{bcd}\\partial_a$, and $\\operatorname{Ric}_{bd}=R^a{}_{bad}$. This is a condition on the supplied metric, not an assertion of existence for prescribed boundary coefficients. Imposing only finitely many asymptotic coefficient equations does not assert membership in this vacuum subclass; formal boundary-data examples must state separately which equations they impose.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
