          "physical_scope": "Conditional coefficient identity for a smooth Ricci-flat Bondi expansion; no global vacuum solution, radiation measurement, or physical validity claim is asserted.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice for the smooth Lorentzian bundle conventions of the suppliers. Let a vacuum Bondi expansion be as in [[def-gr-fx-bondi-expansion]], with $R_{ab}=0$ in the curvature convention of [[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]]. Then, for the mass aspect $m$, shear $C_{AB}$, news $N_{AB}=\\partial_uC_{AB}$, unit sphere metric $q_{AB}$ and its Levi-Civita derivative $D_A$ specified there,\n\n$$\\partial_um=\\frac14D_AD_BN^{AB}-\\frac18N_{AB}N^{AB}.$$\n\nThe identity is the leading supplementary vacuum Einstein coefficient at future null infinity; it is not an exact finite-radius equation.",
