          "physical_scope": "A formal boundary-data example with an exact flat seed and finite shear action; it distinguishes shear from news and does not claim a full transformed vacuum metric or observation.",
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $q_{AB}$ be the unit round metric on $S^2$, $D_A$ its Levi-Civita derivative, and $d\\Omega$ its area form. On $I=\\mathbb R$ and $r>r_0>0$, with $r_0$ a length, the exact flat Bondi metric is $g_0=-du^2-2du\\,dr+r^2q_{AB}dx^A dx^B$; its shear, news and mass aspect are $C_{AB}=N_{AB}=m=0$. Let $m_B(u)=\\tfrac1{4\\pi}\\int_{S^2}m(u,x)\\,d\\Omega$. Let $Y(x)=\\tfrac12(3x_3^2-1)$ on $S^2$, set $f=aY$ for a nonzero length $a$, and use the finite active boundary action $C^{(f)}_{AB}(u,x)=C_{AB}(u+f(x),x)-2D_AD_Bf+q_{AB}D^CD_Cf$, $N^{(f)}_{AB}(u,x)=N_{AB}(u+f(x),x)$. It gives $C^{(f)}_{AB}=-2aT_{AB}$, where $T_{AB}=D_AD_BY-\\tfrac12q_{AB}D^2Y$, and $N^{(f)}_{AB}=0$. Treat these as formal boundary data with $m=0$ and impose the local coefficient constraint $\\partial_um=\\tfrac14D_AD_BN^{AB}-\\tfrac18N_{AB}N^{AB}$. Then $m_B=0$, $dm_B/du=0$, and $\\Delta C_{AB}=0$ on every retarded-time interval, where $\\Delta C_{AB}=C_{AB}(u_2,x)-C_{AB}(u_1,x)$ for $u_1<u_2$. No full finite-transformed vacuum metric is asserted. A nonzero shear value alone therefore does not imply nonzero news or a nonzero shear difference.\n\n",
