          "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $s>0$ and let $g_{\\mathrm{ext}}$ be the\nregular advanced-chart extension of the Schwarzschild exterior, with\n$f(r)=1-s/r$ and stationary field $T=\\partial_v$. Give its domain\n$M_{\\mathrm{ext}}=\\mathbb R_v\\times(0,\\infty)_r\\times S^2$ the product\norientation determined by $dv\\wedge dr\\wedge\\omega_{S^2}$, where\n$\\omega_{S^2}$ is the positive area form of the unit round sphere in its\noutward orientation; write $d\\Omega$ for its associated positive area measure.\nIn this orientation,\n$\\mathrm{vol}_{g_{\\mathrm{ext}}}=r^2\\,dv\\wedge dr\\wedge\\omega_{S^2}$. Let $C$ be a compact finite\nsmooth singular four-chain in the exterior closure $r\\geq s$, with oriented\nboundary\n$\\partial C=\\Sigma_2-\\Sigma_1+\\mathcal H^++B_{\\mathrm{out}}$, where\n$\\Sigma_1,\\Sigma_2$ are spacelike faces with future unit normals $n_1,n_2$,\n$\\mathcal H^+$ is a future-horizon face, and $B_{\\mathrm{out}}$ is the\nremaining signed outer boundary. Let $\\psi$ be smooth on a neighborhood of\n$C$ and solve $\\Box_{g_{\\mathrm{ext}}}\\psi=0$. Define\n$j_T^a:=-Q^{a}{}_{b}[\\psi]T^b$. Orient each spacelike face $\\Sigma_j$ so\nthat its adapted unit normal is the future unit normal $n_j$, and define\n\n$$E_j:=\\Phi_{j_T}(\\Sigma_j)=\\int_{\\Sigma_j}Q_{ab}[\\psi]n_j^aT^b\\,d\\mu_{\\Sigma_j}.$$\n\nDefine $F_{\\mathrm{out}}$ as the signed flux of\n$j_T$ through $B_{\\mathrm{out}}$ and\n$F_H:=\\int_{\\mathcal H^+}(T\\psi)^2\\,d\\mu_H$, where\n$d\\mu_H=s^2\\,dv\\,d\\Omega$ is the positive horizon measure in the advanced\nchart. Then $E_1,E_2,F_H\\geq0$ and\n\n$$E_2+F_H+F_{\\mathrm{out}}=E_1.$$\n\nThe signed outer flux need not be nonnegative. On the exterior static slices\n$x^0=\\text{constant}$, $n=f^{-1/2}T$ and\n$Q(n,T)=\\sqrt f\\,Q(n,n)$; this stationary slice energy degenerates as\n$r\\downarrow s$, where $T$ becomes null in the regular extension.\n\n",
