          "statement": "Take the oriented triangle $v_0\\xrightarrow{e_1}v_1\\xrightarrow{e_2}v_2\\xrightarrow{e_3}v_0$, assign $g_{e_1}=g_{e_2}=g_{e_3}=I_2$, and use the defining representation $\\rho:SU(2)\\to U(\\mathbb C^2)$ given by $\\rho(g)v:=gv$ for column vectors $v\\in\\mathbb C^2$. Let $k=\\operatorname{diag}(i,-i)\\in SU(2)$ and take the vertex gauge assignment $h_{v_0}=k$, $h_{v_1}=h_{v_2}=I_2$. The first and third edge matrices change to $k^{-1}$ and $k$, respectively, while the loop product remains $I_2$ and its Wilson trace remains $2$.\n\n",
