          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $d,e\\ge1$ and let $\\mathcal A$ be a finite nonempty outcome set. A finite completely positive instrument from $\\mathbb C^d$ to $\\mathbb C^e$ is a family of completely positive complex-linear maps $I_a:M_d(\\mathbb C)\\to M_e(\\mathbb C)$, indexed by $a\\in\\mathcal A$, whose sum is trace-preserving. Then there are an integer $q\\ge1$, an isometry $V:\\mathbb C^d\\to\\mathbb C^e\\otimes\\mathbb C^q$, and pairwise orthogonal projections $Q_a$ on $\\mathbb C^q$ with $\\sum_aQ_a=I_q$ such that, for every $X\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$,\n$$\nI_a(X)=\\operatorname{Tr}_E\\!\\left[(I_e\\otimes Q_a)VXV^*(I_e\\otimes Q_a)\\right].\n$$\nHere $E=\\mathbb C^q$ is the finite register space with its displayed orthonormal basis, and the partial trace is defined on its matrix units by $\\operatorname{Tr}_E(Y\\otimes|e_{a,r}\\rangle\\langle e_{b,s}|)=\\delta_{(a,r),(b,s)}Y$, extended linearly. The register basis is indexed by the Kraus labels $(a,r)$; a zero outcome map has no labels and corresponds to $Q_a=0$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
