          "statement": "Input integers $d,m\\ge1$, a finite POVM $(F_a)_{a=1}^m$ on $\\mathbb C^d$ that spans the real Hermitian matrices, and real frequencies $f_a\\ge0$ with $\\sum_af_a=1$. Form the Gram matrix $G_{ab}=\\operatorname{Tr}(F_aF_b)$, compute its Moore–Penrose inverse $G^+$, set $D_a=\\sum_b(G^+)_{ba}F_b$, and return\n$$\nX=\\sum_{a=1}^m f_aD_a.\n$$\nAll sums and matrices are finite. The output is Hermitian. The procedure does not project $X$ onto the positive cone, and it makes no positivity claim for finite frequency inputs.",
