          "library": "mathematics",
          "title": "Laurent subtraction factors a character into counterterm and finite characters",
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal T$ be the isomorphism classes of finite nonempty rooted trees and $H=\\mathbb Q[\\mathcal T]$ their connected graded commutative Hopf algebra, graded by total vertices. Its coproduct is $\\Delta(t)=t\\otimes1+\\sum_C P_C(t)\\otimes R_C(t)$, where $C$ ranges over edge subsets meeting each root-to-leaf path at most once (including the empty cut), $P_C(t)$ is the child-side forest, and $R_C(t)$ is the root-side component; let $S$ be its antipode. Put $H_+=\\bigoplus_{n>0}H_n$. Let $K$ be a commutative unital $\\mathbb Q$-algebra, let $\\epsilon$ be formal, and let $A=K((\\epsilon))=A_-\\oplus A_+$ split into strictly negative and nonnegative powers, with $R$ the projection onto $A_-$. A character is a unital algebra homomorphism $\\phi:H\\to A$. For each positive-degree homogeneous $h$, write $\\widetilde\\Delta(h)=\\Delta(h)-h\\otimes1-1\\otimes h$ and define recursively\n$$B_\\phi(h)=\\phi(h)+\\sum_{\\widetilde\\Delta(h)}\\phi_-(h_{(1)})\\phi(h_{(2)}),\\qquad \\phi_-(1)=1,\\qquad \\phi_-(h)=-R B_\\phi(h).$$\nThe sum is over the finite reduced coproduct and the recursion is degreewise finite. Define convolution by $f*g=m_A(f\\otimes g)\\Delta$, where $m_A$ and $u_A$ are the multiplication and unit maps of $A$, and put $\\phi_+=\\phi_-*\\phi$. Then $\\phi_-$ and $\\phi_+$ are characters, $\\phi_-(H_+)\\subseteq A_-$ and $\\phi_+(H)\\subseteq A_+$, and the convolution inverse $\\phi_-^{-1}=\\phi_-\\circ S$ exists with\n$$\\phi=\\phi_-^{-1}*\\phi_+.$$\nThis is an algebraic factorization for characters; it does not assert a graph-to-rooted-tree identification for actual Feynman graphs.",
