          "library": "mathematics",
          "title": "Abelian local jet BRST differential",
          "statement": "Use the smooth off-shell coordinate model $\\mathbb M=\\mathbb R^4$, with $x^0=c_{\\mathrm{light}}t$ in SI coordinates, metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, increasing $x^0$ as the future direction, and standard orientation. The scalar time-ordering convention sets $c_{\\mathrm{light}}=1$, so $x^0$ is the length coordinate in that convention as well. Here off shell means that no field equation is imposed. Take smooth real components $a_\\mu\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb M;\\mathbb R)$ and a smooth commuting matter field $\\psi\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb M;\\mathbb C^4)$. Use the normalized real potential $a=a_\\mu dx^\\mu$ and dimensionless coupling $g=q\\sqrt{\\mu_0c_{\\mathrm{light}}/\\hbar}$ of the charged-gauge-data convention; $a_\\mu$ has units $\\mathrm m^{-1}$, $g$ is dimensionless, and $\\psi$ has units $\\mathrm m^{-3/2}$. The exact supplier convention is $a'_\\mu=a_\\mu+\\partial_\\mu\\alpha$, $\\psi'=e^{ig\\alpha}\\psi$, for a smooth dimensionless real infinitesimal gauge parameter $\\alpha$.\n\nLet $\\mathcal P$ be the free graded-commutative $\\mathbb C$-algebra over $C^\\infty(\\mathbb M;\\mathbb C)$ generated by the finite jets of $a_\\mu$, $\\psi$, an odd ghost $c_{\\mathrm{gh}}$, an odd antighost $\\bar c$, and an even auxiliary variable $B$. Every element of $\\mathcal P$ is a polynomial in finitely many jet coordinates. The fields $a_\\mu$ and $\\psi$ have Grassmann parity $0$ and ghost number $0$; $c_{\\mathrm{gh}}$ has parity $1$ and ghost number $1$; $\\bar c$ has parity $1$ and ghost number $-1$; and $B$ has parity $0$ and ghost number $0$. The ghost and nonminimal variables are formal algebraic generators; no state-space or positivity claim is made. The generators $c_{\\mathrm{gh}},\\bar c,B$ carry no physical unit assignment, and the differential below is dimensionless. The subscript distinguishes the ghost from the speed of light $c_{\\mathrm{light}}$.\n\nLet $s$ vanish on the coefficient algebra, so $s f=0$ for every $f\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb M;\\mathbb C)$. Thus $s$ is $C^\\infty(\\mathbb M;\\mathbb C)$-linear.\n\nDefine the odd derivation $s:\\mathcal P\\to\\mathcal P$ of ghost number $1$ by\n$$\nsa_\\mu=\\partial_\\mu c_{\\mathrm{gh}},\\qquad sc_{\\mathrm{gh}}=0,\\qquad s\\bar c=B,\\qquad sB=0,\\qquad s\\psi=igc_{\\mathrm{gh}}\\psi .\n$$\nExtend $s$ by the graded Leibniz rule $s(XY)=(sX)Y+(-1)^{|X|}X(sY)$ for homogeneous $X$, where $|X|$ is Grassmann parity, and by $s(\\partial^\\beta X)=\\partial^\\beta(sX)$ for every multi-index $\\beta$. This is an off-shell local algebraic differential for the Abelian gauge transformations; it is not a BRST charge on a Hilbert space and it does not assert existence of a gauge-invariant quantum theory.",
