          "title": "The Schwinger term obeys the Lie cocycle condition",
          "statement": "For the finite-dimensional real Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g$, invariant symmetric form $\\kappa$, smooth loop algebra $\\mathcal L\\mathfrak g$, and bilinear form $\\omega$ defined in [[def-qftx-loop-current-cocycle]], the form $\\omega$ is alternating and satisfies\n$$\\omega([X,Y],Z)+\\omega([Y,Z],X)+\\omega([Z,X],Y)=0\\qquad(X,Y,Z\\in\\mathcal L\\mathfrak g).$$\nConsequently the candidate bracket on $\\widehat{\\mathcal L\\mathfrak g}$ is a Lie bracket and gives a one-dimensional central extension of $\\mathcal L\\mathfrak g$ by $\\mathbb R$.",
