igma,\\mathbf n}=\\operatorname{ran}P_\\sigma(\\mathbf n)$ form smooth complex line subbundles of $S^2\\times\\mathbb C^3$. Here a smooth line subbundle means a family of one-dimensional complex fibers with smooth local unit sections. The common smooth domain for differential calculations is\n\n$$\\mathcal D=\\{f\\in C_c^\\infty(M;\\mathbb C^3):\\mathbf k\\cdot f(\\mathbf k)=0\\text{ for every }\\mathbf k\\in M\\}.$$\n\nIt is dense in $\\mathcal H_T^\\nu$. For $0<r_0<r_1<\\infty$, the mass-shell measure of the radial annulus is $\\nu(\\{r_0\\le|\\mathbf k|\\le r_1\\})=\\pi(r_1^2-r_0^2)$; in particular $\\nu$ is sigma-finite.",
