          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $S^2=\\{\\mathbf n\\in\\mathbb R^3:|\\mathbf n|=1\\}$ with the subspace topology and six smooth graph charts: for $j\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $\\varepsilon\\in\\{+1,-1\\}$, the chart on $\\{\\varepsilon n_j>0\\}$ uses the other coordinates in $B_1^2=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^2:|x|<1\\}$ and has inverse $n_j=\\varepsilon\\sqrt{1-\\sum_{i\\ne j}n_i^2}$. Orient it by the outward unit normal, so an ordered tangent basis $(u,v)$ is positive exactly when $u\\times v=\\lambda\\mathbf n$ for some real $\\lambda>0$; in spherical coordinates away from the poles its area form is $d\\Omega=\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta\\wedge d\\varphi$. In that chart let $\\mathbf n=(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\varphi,\\sin\\theta\\sin\\varphi,\\cos\\theta)$, $\\mathbf e_\\theta=(\\cos\\theta\\cos\\varphi,\\cos\\theta\\sin\\varphi,-\\sin\\theta)$, and $\\mathbf e_\\varphi=(-\\sin\\varphi,\\cos\\varphi,0)$. For $\\sigma\\in\\{+1,-1\\}$ set $e_\\sigma=(\\mathbf e_\\theta+i\\sigma\\mathbf e_\\varphi)/\\sqrt2$, a local unit frame of $\\mathcal L_{\\sigma,\\mathbf n}=\\operatorname{ran}P_\\sigma(\\mathbf n)$. With Hermitian pairing $\\overline u\\cdot v$, define the skew-Hermitian connection form $\\omega_\\sigma=e_\\sigma^\\dagger de_\\sigma$, its curvature $\\Omega_\\sigma=d\\omega_\\sigma$, the real Berry connection $A_\\sigma=-i e_\\sigma^\\dagger de_\\sigma$, and $F_\\sigma=dA_\\sigma$. Then\n$$A_\\sigma=-\\sigma\\cos\\theta\\,d\\varphi,\\qquad F_\\sigma=\\sigma\\sin\\theta\\,d\\theta\\wedge d\\varphi,\\qquad \\frac{1}{2\\pi}\\int_{S^2}F_\\sigma=2\\sigma.$$\nUse the Chern-Weil convention $c_1(\\mathcal L_\\sigma)[S^2]=\\frac{i}{2\\pi}\\int_{S^2}\\Omega_\\sigma$ for $\\nabla=d+\\omega_\\sigma$; then $c_1(\\mathcal L_\\sigma)[S^2]=-2\\sigma$. The north and south unit gauges $e_\\sigma^N=e^{i\\sigma\\varphi}e_\\sigma$ and $e_\\sigma^S=e^{-i\\sigma\\varphi}e_\\sigma$ have transition $e_\\sigma^N=e^{2i\\sigma\\varphi}e_\\sigma^S$; the map $e^{i\\varphi}\\mapsto e^{2i\\sigm