          "strategy": "1.1 The groupoid cardinality and integral in the Definition are finite sums by [A1]. Fix $d\\in\\mathcal D$ and one representative $c$ from each source isomorphism class. The set of isomorphisms $p(c)\\cong d$ is empty or a torsor for the finite group $\\operatorname{Aut}_{\\mathcal D}(d)$. Every object of the homotopy fiber is isomorphic to one with such a chosen source representative, so the fiber has finitely many isomorphism classes. The automorphisms of $(c,\\alpha)$ are the $u\\in\\operatorname{Aut}_{\\mathcal C}(c)$ satisfying $\\alpha\\circ p(u)=\\alpha$, a subgroup of a finite group by [A1]. Thus every homotopy fiber is finite and each pushforward sum is finite. [given, A1]",
