          "statement": "Let $p:\\mathcal X\\to\\mathcal Y$ and $q:\\mathcal Y\\to\\mathcal Z$ be functors of finite groupoids. The iterated homotopy fiber over any $z\\in\\mathcal Z$ is equivalent to the homotopy fiber of $q\\circ p$, so $(q\\circ p)_!=q_!p_!$. Consequently, for composable spans of finite groupoids, the induced push-pull maps compose by the homotopy-pullback composite span. If $\\mathcal X\\xleftarrow{a}\\mathcal E\\xrightarrow{b}\\mathcal Y$ is a span, equip invariant functions with\n\n$$\\langle f,g\\rangle_{\\mathcal X}:=\\sum_{[x]\\in\\pi_0(\\mathcal X)} \\frac{\\overline{f([x])}\\,g([x])}{|\\operatorname{Aut}_{\\mathcal X}(x)|}.$$\n\nThen the adjoint of $b_!a^*$ is $a_!b^*$, the map of the transposed span.",
