          "id": "def-csm-frontier-finite-generator-chain",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite-state generator chain",
          "statement": "Let $E=\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for a finite integer $m\\ge1$. A rate matrix on $E$ is a real matrix $L=(L_{ij})_{i,j\\in E}$ such that $L_{ij}\\ge0$ for $i\\ne j$ and $\\sum_{j\\in E}L_{ij}=0$ for every $i$. Write $\\lambda_i=\\sum_{j\\ne i}L_{ij}$, so $L_{ii}=-\\lambda_i$. The row convention acts on a column observable $f:E\\to\\mathbb R$ by $(Lf)(i)=\\sum_jL_{ij}f(j)$; a row probability vector evolves by right multiplication.\n\nFix an initial probability vector $\\nu=(\\nu_i)_{i\\in E}$, meaning $\\nu_i\\ge0$ and $\\sum_{i\\in E}\\nu_i=1$; initial law $\\nu$ means $\\mathbb P(Y_0=i)=\\nu_i$ for every $i\\in E$. Put $q=\\max_i\\lambda_i$. If $q=0$, then $L=0$ and set $N_t=0$ for every $t\\ge0$ and let the associated realization be the constant process $X_t=Y_0$ with $Y_0\\sim\\nu$. If $q>0$, put $R=I+L/q$, a stochastic matrix. A uniformized realization consists of a probability space carrying a discrete-time Markov sequence $(Y_n)_{n\\ge0}$ with initial law $\\nu$ and transition matrix $R$, and independent random variables $(W_n)_{n\\ge1}$ that are independent of the entire sequence $Y$ and satisfy $\\mathbb P(W_n>u)=e^{-qu}$ for $u\\ge0$. Here a discrete-time Markov sequence with transition matrix $R$ means that\n$$\\mathbb P(A\\cap\\{Y_{n+1}=j\\})=\\mathbb E[\\mathbf1_A R_{Y_nj}]$$\nfor every $n\\ge0$, $j\\in E$, and $A\\in\\sigma(Y_0,\\ldots,Y_n)$. Each $W_n$ therefore has the exponential distribution of rate $q$; in particular its mean is $q^{-1}$. Require $\\sum_{n\\ge1}W_n=+\\infty$ almost surely. Put $T_0=0$, $T_n=\\sum_{k=1}^nW_k$, and, on this probability-one event, $N_t=\\max\\{n:T_n\\le t\\}$ and $X_t=Y_{N_t}$. On its null complement set $N_t=0$ and $X_t=Y_0$. The construction filtration is $\\mathcal F_t=\\sigma(N_s,X_s:0\\le s\\le t)$; it records event counts and states through time $t$ and is not completed or made right-continuous by this definition.\n\nThis uniformized construction permits reducible rate matrices and states with zero exit rate. Under the Axiom of Choice, [[lem-csm-frontier-finite-generator-chain-existence]] proves that every finite rate matrix and initial law admit such a realization and that its conditional transition matrices are $e^{tL}:=\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty t^nL^n/n!$.",
