          "title": "Finite-horizon L2 maximal bound for martingales with right-continuous paths and left limits",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $T\\ge0$, let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ be a probability space, and let $(\\mathcal F_t)_{0\\le t\\le T}$ be an increasing family of sub-$\\sigma$-algebras of $\\mathcal F$. Let $(M_t)_{0\\le t\\le T}$ be a family of real random variables such that each $M_t$ is $\\mathcal F_t$-measurable, $\\mathbb E[M_t^2]<\\infty$, $M_0=0$, and $\\mathbb E[M_t\\mid\\mathcal F_s]=M_s$ almost surely for every $0\\le s\\le t\\le T$. Suppose it has càdlàg paths almost surely, meaning there is a measurable event $\\Omega_0\\in\\mathcal F$ with $\\mathbb P(\\Omega_0)=1$ such that, for every $\\omega\\in\\Omega_0$, the path $t\\mapsto M_t(\\omega)$ is right-continuous on $[0,T)$ and has a finite left limit at every $t\\in(0,T]$. Define\n$$\nD_T=\\bigcup_{n\\ge0}\\{kT/2^n:0\\le k\\le2^n\\},\\qquad S_T=\\sup_{t\\in D_T}|M_t|.\n$$\nThen $S_T$ is measurable and agrees with the pathwise supremum $\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}|M_t|$ on $\\Omega_0$, and\n$$\n\\mathbb E[S_T^2]\\le4\\,\\mathbb E[|M_T|^2].\n$$\n\n",
