          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $E$ be finite and nonempty, let $L$ be a rate matrix on $E$, let $X$ be its uniformized realization from the preceding existence result, and let $f:E\\to\\mathbb R$ be bounded. Put $g=Lf$ and\n$$M_t=f(X_t)-f(X_0)-\\int_0^t g(X_s)\\,ds,\\qquad \\Gamma_f(i)=L(f^2)(i)-2f(i)Lf(i).$$\nFor every finite $T$, $(M_t)_{0\\le t\\le T}$ is a square-integrable martingale relative to the construction filtration, and\n$$A_t:=\\int_0^t\\Gamma_f(X_s)\\,ds$$\nis its continuous predictable bracket: $A_0=0$, $A$ is increasing and predictable, and $M_t^2-A_t$ is a martingale. The bracket is understood in the continuous predictable increasing compensator convention stated in the proof.",
