          "id": "def-csm-frontier-dobrushin-matrix",
          "kind": "definition",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Finite-spin Dobrushin influence matrix",
          "statement": "Let $d\\geq1$, let $S$ be a finite nonempty set, and put $X=S^{\\mathbb Z^d}$ with the $\\sigma$-algebra generated by finite-coordinate cylinders. A specification on $X$ is a family $\\gamma=(\\gamma_\\Lambda)$ of probability kernels indexed by finite $\\Lambda\\subset\\mathbb Z^d$. It is proper when each kernel leaves every exterior-measurable event fixed, and consistent when $\\gamma_\\Lambda\\gamma_\\Delta=\\gamma_\\Lambda$ for all finite $\\Delta\\subseteq\\Lambda$. For $i\\in\\mathbb Z^d$, write $\\gamma_i(\\cdot\\mid\\eta)$ for its one-site conditional probability vector on $S$, where $\\eta\\in S^{\\mathbb Z^d\\setminus\\{i\\}}$. For probability vectors $p,q$ on $S$, define their total-variation distance by $\\lVert p-q\\rVert_{\\rm TV}:=\\frac12\\sum_{s\\in S}|p(s)-q(s)|$. The influence coefficient of site $j$ on the conditional law at site $i$ is\n\n$$c^\\gamma_{ij}:=\\begin{cases}0,&i=j,\\\\[2pt]\\displaystyle\\sup_{\\substack{\\eta,\\eta'\\in S^{\\mathbb Z^d\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\\\ \\eta_k=\\eta'_k\\ \\text{for every }k\\notin\\{i,j\\}}}\\lVert\\gamma_i(\\cdot\\mid\\eta)-\\gamma_i(\\cdot\\mid\\eta')\\rVert_{\\rm TV},&i\\ne j.\\end{cases}$$\n\nThe matrix $C^\\gamma=(c^\\gamma_{ij})_{i,j\\in\\mathbb Z^d}$ is the Dobrushin influence matrix of $\\gamma$. Its coefficients lie in $[0,1]$; a supremum need not be attained. The Dobrushin row constant is $c_\\gamma:=\\sup_i\\sum_j c^\\gamma_{ij}$, with value $+\\infty$ allowed. A common uniform finite influence radius $R$ means $c^\\gamma_{ij}=0$ whenever $\\lVert i-j\\rVert_\\infty>R$.",
