          "title": "Finite Gibbs response of an observable is $\\beta$ times its covariance with the field-coupled observable",
          "statement": "Let $E$ be a finite nonempty set, let $H_0,M,F:E\\to\\mathbb R$, fix $\\beta>0$, and for $t\\in\\mathbb R$ define $H_t(x):=H_0(x)-tM(x)$, $Z(t):=\\sum_{x\\in E}e^{-\\beta H_t(x)}$, and $\\gamma_t(x):=Z(t)^{-1}e^{-\\beta H_t(x)}$. For functions $F,M:E\\to\\mathbb R$, define $\\operatorname{Cov}_{\\gamma_t}(F,M):=\\sum_x\\gamma_t(x)F(x)M(x)-(\\sum_x\\gamma_t(x)F(x))(\\sum_x\\gamma_t(x)M(x))$. Then $t\\mapsto\\sum_x\\gamma_t(x)F(x)$ is differentiable on $\\mathbb R$ and\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\sum_{x\\in E}\\gamma_t(x)F(x)=\\beta\\operatorname{Cov}_{\\gamma_t}(F,M).$$",
