          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $d,L\\ge1$ be integers, let $\\Lambda_{d,L}=(\\mathbb Z/L\\mathbb Z)^d$ have $N=L^d$ sites, and let $\\kappa>0$. Define the zero-mass precision $K:=\\kappa(-\\Delta)$ on $\\mathbb R^{\\Lambda_{d,L}}$, with the periodic Laplacian convention of [[lem-csm-frontier-periodic-laplacian-spectrum]]. Then the unrestricted Lebesgue normalizer diverges:\n\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb R^{\\Lambda_{d,L}}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac12z^{\\mathsf T}Kz\\right)\\,d\\lambda_N(z)=+\\infty.$$\n\nThus this quadratic weight does not define a probability density on the full coordinate space. A finite-volume massless Gaussian must first restrict the field, for example to $\\{z:\\sum_{x\\in\\Lambda_{d,L}}z_x=0\\}$, before inverting the Laplacian.\n\n",
