          "title": "Weak heat solutions on the continuum torus",
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$), meaning every at most countable family of nonempty sets has a choice function. Let $d\\ge1$, let $\\mathbb T^d=(\\mathbb R/\\mathbb Z)^d$ carry the normalized product Haar measure $dx$ with $dx(\\mathbb T^d)=1$, and let $\\rho_0$ be a real measurable function on $\\mathbb T^d$ with $0\\le\\rho_0\\le1$ almost everywhere. For a finite $T\\ge0$, a **weak heat solution with datum $\\rho_0$** is a family $(u_t)_{0\\le t\\le T}$ of real essentially bounded measurable-function classes (elements of $L^\\infty(\\mathbb T^d,dx;\\mathbb R)$), with $u_0=\\rho_0$ as a function class, such that for every complex-valued smooth periodic test function $G$, the map $t\\mapsto\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}u_t(x)G(x)\\,dx$ is continuous and\n\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}u_t(x)G(x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}\\rho_0(x)G(x)\\,dx+\\int_0^t\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}u_s(x)\\Delta G(x)\\,dx\\,ds$$\n\nfor every $0\\le t\\le T$. Here $\\Delta=\\sum_{i=1}^d\\partial_{x_i}^2$ is the periodic Laplacian; equality of function classes means equality almost everywhere with respect to $dx$. For the Fourier convention on this torus, set $e_k(x)=\\exp(2\\pi i k\\cdot x)$ for $k\\in\\mathbb Z^d$ and $\\widehat f(k)=\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}f(x)e_{-k}(x)\\,dx$ for $f\\in L^1(\\mathbb T^d,dx)$.",
