rns a non-finite status, return unresolved-operation and no finite enclosure claim. Otherwise return the finite intervals $\\mathcal Z$ and $\\mathcal N$. If the lower endpoint of $\\mathcal Z$ is strictly positive, also return the outward interval quotient $\\mathcal E=\\mathcal N/\\mathcal Z$; if that endpoint is nonpositive, return unresolved-denominator and no normalized-expectation enclosure.\n\nThis is finite enumeration and can require exponentially many operations in the model size. It certifies arithmetic from supplied weight intervals; it does not certify how those intervals were obtained.",
