          "physical_scope": null,
          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $0<p<1$ and $\\rho=\\operatorname{diag}(p,1-p)$ on $\\mathbb C^2$. Its modular automorphism group acts on the off-diagonal matrix unit by\n$$\\sigma_t(E_{12})=e^{it\\log(p/(1-p))}E_{12}.$$\nThe modular frequency $\\log(p/(1-p))$ is dimensionless and does not specify a physical energy or clock. If one separately supplies a Hamiltonian $H=\\operatorname{diag}(E_1,E_2)$ with energies in joules, inverse energy $\\beta>0$ in joules$^{-1}$, and action $\\hbar>0$ in joule-seconds with $\\rho=e^{-\\beta H}/Z$, then $p/(1-p)=e^{-\\beta(E_1-E_2)}$ and the physical angular frequency $(E_1-E_2)/\\hbar$ has units seconds$^{-1}$. For $p=\\tfrac12$ the modular frequency is zero; for $p\\ne\\tfrac12$ it is nonzero but still has no physical time unit before this identification.",
