,\\qquad \\mu=\\frac{ag}{2v+g}>0.$$\n\nThis is exponential connected clustering for the infinite-volume state. The hypotheses do not require uniformly gapped finite-volume approximations, translation invariance, or a particular choice of finite-volume boundary ground states. The same estimate holds for any positive-energy state representation with $\\ker K=\\mathbb C\\Omega$ and the stated gap, even without uniqueness among all ground states. Uniqueness is a sufficient hypothesis for that kernel condition, proved below. For other weighted interactions the assertion applies whenever their strongly continuous dynamics and the displayed Lieb–Robinson estimate are supplied; no missing thermodynamic-existence theorem for a general interaction is assumed to have been proved here.\n\nFor physical bookkeeping $t$ is in seconds, $H,\\gamma$ are in joules, $\\hbar$ is in joule-seconds and $K,g,v$ have inverse-second units. Lattice distances, $a,C,\\mu$ and the exponential argument are dimensionless. The theorem does not prove a gap or uniqueness for an unspecified physical model.",
