          "physical_scope": null,
          "statement": "Let $d\\geq1$, let $H=H^*\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$ have entries in joules and a finite spectral decomposition $H=\\sum_E E P_E$ with pairwise orthogonal projections summing to $I_d$, and let $S_1,\\ldots,S_m$ be a finite family of dimensionless Hermitian matrices, where $m\\geq0$. Set $\\Omega_H=\\{(E'-E)/\\hbar:E,E'\\in\\operatorname{spec}(H)\\}$ and, for each $\\omega\\in\\Omega_H$, define $S_a(\\omega)=\\sum_{E'-E=\\hbar\\omega}P_E S_aP_{E'}$. Suppose that the rate matrices $\\Gamma(\\omega)=(\\gamma_{ab}(\\omega))$, $\\omega\\in\\Omega_H$, have entries in seconds$^{-1}$, are positive semidefinite in the explicit sense that $\\Gamma(\\omega)=\\Gamma(\\omega)^*$ and $v^*\\Gamma(\\omega)v\\geq0$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb C^m$, and satisfy $\\gamma_{ab}(-\\omega)=e^{-\\beta\\hbar\\omega}\\gamma_{ba}(\\omega)$, with $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$ in joules$^{-1}$ and $\\hbar>0$ in joule-seconds. Let $H_{\\rm LS}=H_{\\rm LS}^*$ have entries in joules and commute with $H$, and let $\\mathcal L$ be the finite generator\n\n$$\\mathcal L(X)=-\\frac{i}{\\hbar}[H+H_{\\rm LS},X]+\\sum_{\\omega\\in\\Omega_H}\\sum_{a,b=1}^{m}\\gamma_{ab}(\\omega)\\left(S_b(\\omega)X S_a(\\omega)^*-\\frac12\\{S_a(\\omega)^*S_b(\\omega),X\\}\\right).$$\n\nFor $\\rho\\in M_d(\\mathbb C)$, being a density matrix means $\\rho=\\rho^*$, $v^*\\rho v\\geq0$ for every $v\\in\\mathbb C^d$, and $\\operatorname{Tr}\\rho=1$; it is faithful when it is positive definite. For $Z_\\beta:=\\operatorname{Tr}(e^{-\\beta H})>0$, define the faithful Gibbs density $\\sigma_\\beta:=e^{-\\beta H}/Z_\\beta$. For time $t\\geq0$ measured in seconds, $T_t:=e^{t\\mathcal L}$ is completely positive and trace-preserving, and $T_t(\\sigma_\\beta)=\\sigma_\\beta$. This statement asserts stationarity only; it asserts neither uniqueness of the stationary density nor convergence to $\\sigma_\\beta$.\n\n",
