          "statement": "Use the finite open or periodic chain and bond-current definition in [[def-qsmx-lattice-current-and-limits]]. Each $j_{j,j+1}$ is self-adjoint, and with $\\dot q_j:=(i/\\hbar)[H_L,q_j]$ the exact local identity\n$$\\dot q_j=j_{j-1,j}-j_{j,j+1}$$\nholds at every site. Consequently the total charge $Q_L:=\\sum_{j\\in\\Lambda_L}q_j$, where $\\Lambda_L$ is the open-chain site set or periodic site set from the definition, is conserved: $[H_L,Q_L]=0$. The current orientation is from $j$ to $j+1$, so positive outgoing current lowers the charge at site $j$.",
