          "id": "def-qsmx-transverse-ising-majoranas",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Open transverse Ising chain and ordered Majorana operators",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "library": "physics",
          "statement": "Let $N\\ge1$ be an integer and let $\\mathcal H_N=(\\mathbb C^2)^{\\otimes N}$ with the product inner product linear in its first argument. At each factor use\n$$\nX=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad Y=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\i&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad Z=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad I_2=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\nFor $1\\le j\\le N$, $X_j,Y_j,Z_j$ denote these matrices on factor $j$ and $I_2$ on every other factor. For real $h,J$ measured in joules define the finite open-chain matrix\n$$H_N(h,J)=-h\\sum_{j=1}^N Z_j-J\\sum_{j=1}^{N-1}X_jX_{j+1}.$$\nThe upper limit $N-1$ is the open-boundary convention: no term couples site $N$ to site $1$. Put $S_0=I_{\\mathcal H_N}$ and $S_{j-1}=Z_1\\cdots Z_{j-1}$ for $j>1$. The ordered Majorana operators are\n$$\\gamma_{2j-1}=S_{j-1}X_j,\\qquad \\gamma_{2j}=S_{j-1}Y_j\\qquad(1\\le j\\le N).$$",
          "deps": [
