          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $h,J\\in\\mathbb R$ be energies in joules, with the convention of the open-chain definition: the field coefficient is $h$ and the adjacent-site bond coefficient is $J$, with no bond joining the final site to the first. On $\\mathcal K=\\ell^2(\\mathbb Z;\\mathbb C^2)$, write $x_j=(u_j,v_j)$ and define the everywhere-defined complex-linear operator $A_\\infty:\\mathcal K\\to\\mathcal K$ by\n$$ (A_\\infty x)_j=\\bigl(2h v_j-2Jv_{j-1},\\,-2h u_j+2Ju_{j+1}\\bigr),\\qquad K_\\infty=iA_\\infty. $$\nFor any bounded operator $T$ on the Hilbert space $\\mathcal K$, let $T^*$ denote its Hilbert adjoint. Use the Fourier unitary $\\mathcal F x(k)=\\sum_jx_je^{ijk}$ on $\\mathbb T=\\mathbb R/(2\\pi\\mathbb Z)$ with normalized measure. Define the continuous matrix symbol\n$$M(k)=\\begin{pmatrix}0&2i(h-Je^{ik})\\\\-2i(h-Je^{-ik})&0\\end{pmatrix},$$\nwhose eigenvalues are $\\pm\\epsilon(k)$, where\n$$\\epsilon(k)=2\\sqrt{h^2+J^2-2hJ\\cos k}.$$\nFor a $2\\times2$ matrix $C$ acting on the defined $\\mathbb C^2$, write $\\|C\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}:=\\sup\\{\\|Cv\\|_{\\mathbb C^2}:\\|v\\|_{\\mathbb C^2}=1\\}$. Then $\\|M(k)\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=2|h-Je^{ik}|\\le2(|h|+|J|)$. Define $\\mathsf M:L^2(\\mathbb T;\\mathbb C^2)\\to L^2(\\mathbb T;\\mathbb C^2)$ by $(\\mathsf Mf)(k)=M(k)f(k)$ almost everywhere. This is an everywhere-defined bounded multiplication operator, and $\\mathcal F K_\\infty\\mathcal F^{-1}=\\mathsf M$.\nBy the stated resolvent convention, $\\lambda\\in\\sigma(K_\\infty)$ exactly when $\\lambda I_{\\mathcal K}-K_\\infty$ has no bounded everywhere-defined two-sided inverse on $\\mathcal K$. Its spectrum is exactly $\\bigcup_{k\\in\\mathbb T}\\{-\\epsilon(k),\\epsilon(k)\\}$. The nonnegative band is $\\epsilon(\\mathbb T)$, whose minimum is\n$$\\Delta_{\\mathrm{bulk}}=\\min_k\\epsilon(k)=2\\bigl||h|-|J|\\bigr|,$$\nso this one-particle band closes exactly when $|h|=|J|$. This statement does not assert uniqueness of an infinite spin-chain ground state or a thermodynamic-limit singularity.\n\n",
          "deps": [
            "def-bounded-linear-operator",
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-hilbert-space-adjoint",
