          },
          "physical_scope": null,
          "statement": "Let $M$ be a smooth $n$-manifold, meaning a topological $n$-manifold equipped with a maximal smooth atlas, and let $\\omega\\in\\Omega^1(M)$ be a smooth real one-form, meaning a smooth section of the cotangent bundle $T^*M\\to M$. Let $\\gamma:[0,1]\\to M$ be a continuous piecewise-$C^1$ curve with $\\gamma(0)=\\gamma(1)$: there is a finite subdivision $0=t_0<\\cdots<t_m=1$ such that on each closed piece a chart contains the curve image, its coordinate representative is $C^1$ on the piece interior, and its derivative extends continuously to the endpoints. At a piece endpoint, use the corresponding one-sided derivative as the tangent. On each piece, pair this tangent $\\dot\\gamma(t)\\in T_{\\gamma(t)}M$ with $\\omega_{\\gamma(t)}\\in T^*_{\\gamma(t)}M$. Define the oriented period by\n\n$$\\operatorname{Per}_\\gamma(\\omega):=\\sum_j\\int_{t_j}^{t_{j+1}}\\omega_{\\gamma(t)}(\\dot\\gamma(t))\\,dt,$$\n\nwhere $0=t_0<\\cdots<t_m=1$ is any admissible chartwise subdivision with the regularity specified above. The covector-vector pairing is intrinsic, and additivity makes this value independent of further subdivision. No invariance under homotopy is asserted by this definition.\n\n",
          "provenance": {
