          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-tgr-charged-liouville-data": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-closed-and-exact-differential-forms": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "physical_scope": null,
          "statement": "Let $O$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian domain, let $\\xi$ be a smooth future-timelike Killing field on $O$, and let $A$ be a global smooth one-form with $F=dA$. Suppose a global smooth scalar $\\Lambda_\\xi$ satisfies $\\mathcal L_\\xi A=d\\Lambda_\\xi$. Define $\\Psi_\\xi:=\\xi^aA_a-\\Lambda_\\xi$ and $\\omega:=\\iota_\\xi F$, with $(\\iota_\\xi F)_a=\\xi^bF_{ba}$. Then\n\n$$\\omega=-d\\Psi_\\xi,$$\n\nso $\\omega$ is exact. This identity uses the global potential symmetry and assumes no charged trajectory or conservation law.",
